# Project:   dfe-docker
# File:      .dockerignore
# Purpose:   Build-context exclusions for any image built with this repo as context
# Language:  dockerignore
#
# License:   BUSL-1.1
# Copyright: (c) 2026 HYPERI PTY LIMITED
#
# Nothing in this repo currently builds with the repo root as its context:
# scripts/build_dev_images.py stages each component's source into a temp dir with
# its own STAGE_EXCLUDES, and the runtime image comes from the component repo's
# own Dockerfile. So today this file is a guard, not a fix.
#
# It earns its keep the moment someone adds a root-context build -- which is
# exactly when nobody remembers to write one, and secrets (.env, env/) get
# shipped into an image layer. That is the failure this prevents.

# Secrets and local config -- the reason this file exists at all.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
env/
certs/

# Version control and CI metadata
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitleaks.toml

# Agent and editor artefacts
.claude/
.hyperi-ai/
.mcp.json
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local build and runtime state
.profile.mk
.tmp/
tmp/
**/target/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Docs and packaging that never belong in a runtime image
docs/
*.md
LICENSE
robots.txt

# Compose definitions themselves -- an image built from this context does not
# need the stack that runs it.
docker-compose*.yml
